p": [["ic", -4.971151065547019e-05], [" ic", -11.010835647583008]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -8.094638178590685e-05, "top": [["px", -8.094638178590685e-05], [" px", -11.193365097045898]]}, {"t": "`)", "lp": -0.023259539157152176, "top": [["`)", -0.023259539157152176], ["`", -4.488412380218506]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -0.29703232645988464, "top": [[" |", -0.29703232645988464], [" \u2014", -1.3637207746505737]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.10259923338890076, "top": [["\n", -0.10259923338890076], ["\n\n", -2.3279294967651367]]}, {"t": "|", "lp": -0.0007230868795886636, "top": [["|", -0.0007230868795886636], [" |", -9.615983963012695]]}, {"t": " `-", "lp": -0.002981274388730526, "top": [[" `-", -0.002981274388730526], [" `", -5.9577484130859375]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed compile doesn't continue silently.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **S**ource directory \u2014 where the source code lives |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **B**uild directory \u2014 where build artifacts go |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** generator (fast, parallel build system) instead of Make |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize for performance (`-O3`, strip debug info) rather than a debug build |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where files will eventually install (standard system location) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Libraries go in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C** compiler (`icx`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel's **C++** compiler (`icpx`) |\n| `-"}